== Implementation (2026-11-06) ==
backend/requirements.txt: fastapi 0.162.0, starlette 1.10.0 (pinned, was transitive), python-multipart 0.0.33.
backend/app/security.py: client_ip_header(), _header_client() (exactly one header line holding one valid IP),
  identity_is_trusted(), client_key() consults only CLIENT_IP_HEADER when it is set (X-Forwarded-For is then never
  read) and only from a TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS peer; proxy_trust_summary() adds "client_identity" (a source, never an
  address). AnalysisMemoryGateMiddleware: max_waiting (MAX_WAITING_UPLOADS, default 2) -> 503 SERVER_BUSY with
  Retry-After for an upload that would wait behind that many; with a trusted identity, a client with an upload
  waiting or running gets 429 ONE_AT_A_TIME with Retry-After; keys held in memory per ticket and dropped in the
  finally.
backend/app/pharmcat_runner.py: non-zero exit -> PharmcatExecutionError (503 PHARMCAT_UNAVAILABLE), operator log
  line with the status only (PharmCAT's stdout/stderr never logged); remove_workdir(): rmtree, one retry, warning per
  failed attempt and an error if the tree survives, naming only the random directory name; module logger
  pharmaguard.pharmcat.
backend/app/main.py: max_waiting passed to the gate.
render.yaml / infra/DEPLOY_NOTES.md: MAX_WAITING_UPLOADS=2, TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=10.0.0.0/8,
  CLIENT_IP_HEADER=cf-connecting-ip documented as intended production values, not auto-applied.
The client needs no change: it shows the server's own sentence for a 429, under the existing heading.

